        "subject": "LU-21059 tests: do not chain the script EXIT trap in a test",
        "message": "LU-21059 tests: do not chain the script EXIT trap in a test\n\nA stack_trap EXIT in a test also runs the EXIT trap of the test\nscript when the test ends.  Thus large-lun test_2 and test_5 run\ncleanupall.  In sanity-lnet, a test trap runs cleanup_testsuite.  If\nthe suite starts with Lustre mounted, cleanup_testsuite calls\nsetupall, and the later tests fail.\n\nrun_one runs each test in a subshell.  The subshell does not run the\nEXIT trap of the script.  But \"trap -p\" in the subshell still prints\nthat trap.  Then stack_trap reads the output and adds the script trap\nto the test trap.\n\nClear the EXIT trap at the start of run_one.  Add sanity-lnet test_30\nto check that a test EXIT trap holds only the test commands.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 1dfda720c080 (\"LU-9474 tests: add the stack_trap() utility function\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Icce49bf560d1f0eeb8de734465e42bf80b15105b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
